1
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,140
My girl's going to be a bride,

2
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:11,520
to get a husband.

3
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:14,680
But Qamar dear, you mustn't talk to anyone.

4
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:16,500
You mustn't even say

5
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:18,300
you're knitting your baby a sweater, OK?

6
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:19,370
OK.

7
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:21,700
Good girl! What a sweet girl!

8
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:23,550
What a sensible girl!

9
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:25,840
Oh, bless

10
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:27,460
that lovely moon face of yours!

11
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:29,800
In front of them, you sit like a lady

12
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,220
and don't say a word.

13
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:34,000
Whatever they ask, let us answer, OK?

14
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:34,840
OK.

15
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,420
You see, Qamar dear,

16
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:38,780
people like a girl to be shy,

17
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:40,040
to keep quiet.

18
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:41,620
If you talk,

19
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:43,670
your husband will leave,

20
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:45,560
then your baby won't have a daddy.

21
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:46,700
Understand, dear?

22
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,600
I love my baby very much.

23
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:50,220
Its sweater's almost done.

24
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:51,980
I hope it has its daddy's hair,

25
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:54,960
long and thick and black.

26
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:00,160
We took Aspiran to Lalehzar and bought him a very smart suit.

27
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:02,480
He looked just like Rudolph Valentino.

28
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:03,680
They're here!

29
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,460
They're here!

30
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:06,920
They're here!

31
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:07,920
Ah, ah.

32
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,040
What is it, Mash Ghasem?

33
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:10,460
They're here!

34
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:13,380
Our townsman isn't wearing his wig!

35
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:14,515
What?

36
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:15,900
Then what's he got on?

37
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:17,620
His own hat, Sir!

38
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,580
Huh! What a donkey!

39
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:23,185
Run, get it off him and bring him here!

40
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:25,620
His old mother's a frightful sight, Sir.

41
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:27,980
We're afraid she'll scare Miss Qamar.

42
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:30,380
We ourselves aren't scared of the English,

43
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:31,980
but she scared us!

44
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:34,520
Why? What's wrong with her? Is she veiled?

45
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:35,880
Come on, say it!

46
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,880
Never mind her veil and wraps,

47
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:39,280
it's the look of her!

48
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,510
The look of her?

49
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:43,740
Honestly, Sir, why lie? The grave is

50
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:45,220
this close!

51
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:47,840
His mother, we saw her ourselves,

52
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:49,320
heaven forbid,

53
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:53,185
she's got a beard and mustache like Seyyed Abolghasem the preacher!

54
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:58,310
Couldn't he have left this beauty queen at home?

55
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:00,080
Mash Ghasem, keep them out of the parlor.

56
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:03,810
Take his mother and sister to the gazebo, give them tea and sweets.

57
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:07,860
He agreed this afternoon, the donkey. His mother must've stopped him.

58
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:10,810
Now if he comes without his wig...

59
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:12,070
Oh, no!

60
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:13,410
That won't do!

61
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:17,320
Why are you just standing there?

62
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:19,320
Asdollah, I'd die for you,

63
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,429
think of something!

64
00:04:20,479 --> 00:04:23,320
Since this morning, my poor girl

65
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:25,320
has talked of nothing but the groom's black hair.

66
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:26,190
Talk him round somehow,

67
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:28,010
to put that wig at least for today

68
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:29,650
on his damn head!

69
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:32,270
Moment... moment... let me go see what can be done.

70
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:33,950
You take Qamar into the parlor.

71
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,350
After a few minutes, have someone call her out.

72
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:39,360
And don't let Qamar go near them again.

73
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:41,970
Qamar dear,

74
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:45,320
once you're tidied up, you'll go into the parlor with your mom.

75
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:47,320
You'll sit a bit with the groom's mother,

76
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:49,320
then you'll come out, OK?

77
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:51,310
But don't say a word about the baby.

78
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:53,320
They mustn't know you're having a baby,

79
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:56,050
or they'll leave, and then you'll be all alone.

80
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:57,320
Understand, sweetheart?

81
00:04:57,360 --> 00:05:01,320
Yes, Uncle Asdollah. I won't mention my baby in front of anyone.

82
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:02,230
Bless that face!

83
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:05,585
Good girl! Bless an obedient girl like you!

84
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:19,090
My respects, Sir.

85
00:05:19,140 --> 00:05:21,330
Well, well, bravo! Hats off to you!

86
00:05:21,380 --> 00:05:22,750
The nerve! What is this?

87
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:25,120
Aspiran, where's your wig?

88
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:27,020
Sir, you must forgive us.

89
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:30,100
Our mom said if we wear the wig, she'll disown us.

90
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:30,940
Well, yes.

91
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:33,670
Man, if you don't wear it, the bride will disown you!

92
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:34,450
Can't, Sir.

93
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:37,415
We don't go against our mom's word.

94
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:39,450
Mash Ghasem, where's the wig now?

95
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:42,245
Here it is. Here you go, Sir.

96
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:43,630
Bring the tea, Mash Ghasem.

97
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:44,700
Yes, Sir.

98
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:46,310
Man, how many times must I say-

99
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:48,320
Excuse me? Now you're playing hard to get?

100
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:49,320
What's wrong with this wig?

101
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:53,250
What would happen if you put it on?

102
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:54,320
Would it hurt to look handsome?

103
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:55,320
She won't allow it.

104
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:59,130
Come, introduce me to your mother... come on, introduce me.

105
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:00,360
Yes, Sir.

106
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:03,360
This here's our mom.

107
00:06:04,668 --> 00:06:06,153
Hello, ma'am.

108
00:06:08,008 --> 00:06:09,598
My respects, ma'am.

109
00:06:09,648 --> 00:06:11,308
You are most, most welcome.

110
00:06:11,358 --> 00:06:13,298
Sir, I'm talking to you.

111
00:06:14,850 --> 00:06:17,180
S... s... sorry, ma'am.

112
00:06:17,448 --> 00:06:19,063
Welcome.

113
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,200
And this is Akhtar, our sister.

114
00:06:25,248 --> 00:06:26,343
Huh?

115
00:06:27,270 --> 00:06:29,950
Oh! What a pretty lady!

116
00:06:30,048 --> 00:06:31,338
Lovely.

117
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:33,428
Let me see.

118
00:06:34,748 --> 00:06:37,663
Let me, let me, let me. Lovely, lovely.

119
00:06:40,048 --> 00:06:41,338
Lovely.

120
00:06:45,928 --> 00:06:48,488
Very, very pleased to meet you, ma'am.

121
00:06:50,548 --> 00:06:54,243
Oh my, to have such a pretty daughter...

122
00:06:56,788 --> 00:07:01,948
I must tell you, I don't like this fancy nonsense one bit.

123
00:07:02,028 --> 00:07:04,338
I raised a son as fresh as a bouquet,

124
00:07:04,388 --> 00:07:05,900
a fine, strapping lad,

125
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:07,980
a joy to look at.

126
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:09,760
Is my boy some dandy

127
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,520
to go wearing a wig?

128
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,695
No, sir, you've got another thing coming!

129
00:07:14,288 --> 00:07:15,120
My boy

130
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:17,400
has nothing wrong with him.

131
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,940
He has a job.

132
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,700
He's respectable.

133
00:07:20,740 --> 00:07:22,520
He even did six grades of school.

134
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:25,520
So he's lost his hair, that's no flaw.

135
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,940
A hundred girls

136
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:28,340
would beg for him.

137
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:30,500
No, my dear sir, this fancy nonsense

138
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:32,675
doesn't suit our family.

139
00:07:33,468 --> 00:07:35,668
What did you people think?

140
00:07:36,028 --> 00:07:37,773
Moment... madam.

141
00:07:37,888 --> 00:07:39,060
What? What?

142
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:42,260
"Moment, moment" means hold on, please.

143
00:07:43,268 --> 00:07:46,400
When you say you raised a son,

144
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:49,220
pardon me, it makes one laugh.

145
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:51,980
Excuse me? What's that supposed to mean?

146
00:07:52,020 --> 00:07:53,180
What do you mean?

147
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:57,040
Am I some freak that I can't have a son?

148
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,740
So now it doesn't suit us?

149
00:07:58,780 --> 00:08:01,080
Who says we can't have a son? Huh?

150
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:06,560
No, madam, you may have a son, just not one this big!

151
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,400
It doesn't suit you at all.

152
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:13,060
How can anyone believe you'd have a son this age?

153
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:15,360
Honestly, between us, who'd believe it?

154
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:18,180
No, it doesn't suit you at all.

155
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:21,135
I swear on your life, on Miss Akhtar's life,

156
00:08:21,868 --> 00:08:23,080
who's like a sister to me,

157
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:24,960
at first I thought you were joking.

158
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,700
I can't believe you're Mr. Aspiran's mother.

159
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:32,360
How could someone as young as you

160
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:35,185
have a son this big!

161
00:08:35,868 --> 00:08:37,060
No, it's impossible.

162
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:40,980
Oh, bless you, the things you men say!

163
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:42,130
No, it's the truth.

164
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:43,640
You know,

165
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:47,260
I was very little when they married me off.

166
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:49,920
I didn't even know what a husband was,

167
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,560
what you do with one,

168
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,140
what he's good for.

169
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:56,240
But Aspiran's late father, God rest him,

170
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:58,160
taught me everything.

171
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:59,160
Yes.

172
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:00,958
Thirteen...

173
00:09:01,008 --> 00:09:02,150
I was fourteen

174
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:04,160
when I had Aspiran.

175
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:06,660
The poor boy isn't that old, you know.

176
00:09:06,868 --> 00:09:10,218
He's had so many troubles in life,

177
00:09:10,268 --> 00:09:12,160
my poor boy's aged before his time.

178
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,160
Don't you fret, madam.

179
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:16,160
Believe me,

180
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:18,160
on your life, on Miss Akhtar's life,

181
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:20,160
even if Mr. Aspiran were only twenty,

182
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:23,375
I wouldn't believe you were his mother.

183
00:09:24,048 --> 00:09:25,160
Besides,

184
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:29,120
you don't even wear powder and lipstick.

185
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:32,460
If you did, what a dish you'd be!

186
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:36,300
Oh, get away with you!

187
00:09:38,628 --> 00:09:40,560
You cheeky devil!

188
00:09:41,348 --> 00:09:42,718
Shazdeh dear.

189
00:09:42,768 --> 00:09:43,928
Yes?

190
00:09:44,428 --> 00:09:49,040
May I ask how you're related to the bride?

191
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:52,440
Well, we're cousins.

192
00:09:54,248 --> 00:09:57,298
Ooh, what a fun relative we've found!

193
00:09:57,348 --> 00:09:58,400
Oh my!

194
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:00,965
Oh, what a lovely mama you have!

195
00:10:03,468 --> 00:10:05,400
Oh, Miss Akhtar, a widow!

196
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:08,290
What a waste for you to stay a widow, oh God!

197
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:10,938
Oh, forget relatives, we're more than that now!

198
00:10:10,988 --> 00:10:16,488
Oh, why didn't you introduce us sooner?

199
00:10:37,588 --> 00:10:40,048
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

200
00:10:47,028 --> 00:10:48,383
Ladies,

201
00:10:49,208 --> 00:10:50,498
gentlemen,

202
00:10:51,828 --> 00:10:56,320
now that you've all blessed this happy union,

203
00:10:58,068 --> 00:11:00,203
I'd like to say a few words

204
00:11:00,968 --> 00:11:07,800
about the standing of our great and exceptional family

205
00:11:08,568 --> 00:11:12,480
to the groom's family.

206
00:11:14,728 --> 00:11:17,980
Madam, honored mother of Mr. Aspiran,

207
00:11:21,728 --> 00:11:23,278
Mr. Groom,

208
00:11:27,668 --> 00:11:29,520
and Miss Akhtar,

209
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:35,060
I congratulate you all on this happy union,

210
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:39,880
and I hope the bride and groom grow old together.

211
00:11:40,488 --> 00:11:42,560
I'm very glad

212
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:46,400
that, as head of the bride's family,

213
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,680
with you...

214
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:49,060
Sir!

215
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:50,098
Sir!

216
00:11:50,148 --> 00:11:51,078
Sir!

217
00:11:51,128 --> 00:11:52,613
What is it, Ghasem?

218
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:54,200
What's happened?

219
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:59,480
We just saw Miss Farrokh Lagha with our own eyes, she's coming, Sir!

220
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:02,380
We don't know how to send her away.

221
00:12:02,420 --> 00:12:05,480
Ghasem, can't you see we have guests?

222
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:07,780
Go tell her no one's home.

223
00:12:09,492 --> 00:12:10,880
What is it? What's going on?

224
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:11,520
Mash Ghasem!

225
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:14,800
Honestly, Sir, we seem to have lost our wits completely.

226
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:20,240
Farrokh Lagha, the jinxed chatterbox once meant to marry Dustali Khan,

227
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,870
was Aziz-Saltaneh's enemy.

228
00:12:23,492 --> 00:12:29,000
With her, the whole town would hear of Qamar's wedding and the groom's roots.

229
00:12:29,872 --> 00:12:31,980
No doubt Agha Jan had tipped her off.

230
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:34,285
We have to clear these away.

231
00:12:34,832 --> 00:12:36,822
Agha Joon! Miss Farrokh Lagha!

232
00:12:36,872 --> 00:12:39,602
Eh, this woman always turns up at the wrong time!

233
00:12:39,652 --> 00:12:41,282
Does this make any sense?

234
00:12:41,332 --> 00:12:47,162
Just when we're having a private family talk, she goes visiting!

235
00:12:47,212 --> 00:12:49,182
Scurrying about like a mouse on fire.

236
00:12:49,232 --> 00:12:51,422
She must be bringing some damn news again.

237
00:12:51,472 --> 00:12:52,582
Let me see.

238
00:12:52,632 --> 00:12:54,542
Madam, don't come in.

239
00:12:54,592 --> 00:12:57,022
Why should I lie? The grave is this close!

240
00:12:57,072 --> 00:12:58,460
Sir has gone to the station.

241
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,640
Don't lie, now.

242
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:02,940
Sir, has something happened?

243
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:05,580
If there's news, tell us too, you hear?

244
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,840
No, no, excuse me, madam.

245
00:13:08,492 --> 00:13:10,692
She's one of our relatives.

246
00:13:11,512 --> 00:13:14,320
A jinxed woman, bad luck wherever she goes.

247
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:17,002
Don't come in, madam, nobody's home.

248
00:13:17,052 --> 00:13:19,002
I can hear him talking.

249
00:13:19,052 --> 00:13:20,480
They've all gone to meet Master Pouri.

250
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:23,762
Why not pop over to the station while it's early?

251
00:13:23,812 --> 00:13:26,980
Well, well!

252
00:13:27,020 --> 00:13:29,020
What a match!

253
00:13:31,020 --> 00:13:31,980
Yes, yes.

254
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:33,980
Let us have some sweets too.

255
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:36,020
Congratulations, God willing.

256
00:13:36,070 --> 00:13:36,722
Thanks.

257
00:13:36,772 --> 00:13:38,980
I heard it's the engagement party today.

258
00:13:39,020 --> 00:13:40,980
Well, nothing's settled yet.

259
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:42,980
God willing, it's good news.

260
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:45,980
Is this the groom's mother?

261
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:47,980
Congratulations, God willing.

262
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:48,980
Bless you.

263
00:13:49,020 --> 00:13:52,922
You won't find a bride this fine in the whole town.

264
00:13:52,972 --> 00:13:56,020
Kind, pretty, house-proud, modest.

265
00:13:57,332 --> 00:14:00,272
By the way, what does the groom do?

266
00:14:00,352 --> 00:14:02,162
At your service, ma'am.

267
00:14:02,232 --> 00:14:04,890
He's an officer with the police.

268
00:14:04,930 --> 00:14:05,980
You're too kind, ma'am.

269
00:14:06,020 --> 00:14:08,020
Well! Congratulations.

270
00:14:09,532 --> 00:14:12,187
His face looks familiar to me.

271
00:14:12,772 --> 00:14:15,167
By the way, how much do you earn?

272
00:14:15,652 --> 00:14:17,917
Miss Farrokh Lagha, about what's-his-name...

273
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:19,970
Has the poor man passed away?

274
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:24,972
Who? Oh, Mobin-Hozour? Yes, poor man had a stroke.

275
00:14:25,020 --> 00:14:26,980
You have every right to be upset.

276
00:14:27,020 --> 00:14:29,350
God rest him, he was a good man.

277
00:14:30,252 --> 00:14:32,692
Did you know he was a distant relative of ours?

278
00:14:32,732 --> 00:14:33,532
No.

279
00:14:33,572 --> 00:14:35,212
The memorial's tomorrow,

280
00:14:35,392 --> 00:14:38,362
Majd Mosque, five in the afternoon.

281
00:14:38,412 --> 00:14:41,012
Do drop by. It'd be nice if Sir came.

282
00:14:41,052 --> 00:14:42,797
As you wish.

283
00:14:43,472 --> 00:14:45,822
We'll certainly come, ma'am.

284
00:14:45,872 --> 00:14:48,502
By the way, madam, is the groom's father living?

285
00:14:48,552 --> 00:14:49,762
No, dear.

286
00:14:49,812 --> 00:14:52,620
Their father died when these two were little.

287
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:53,940
What did he do?

288
00:14:53,980 --> 00:14:58,680
He was a landowner from Qom, with estates in Ghias Abad.

289
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:02,960
Really, madam, such talk is beneath us.

290
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,740
What need is there?

291
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:10,300
No, dear sir, I'm telling the truth so there's no quarreling later.

292
00:15:10,340 --> 00:15:13,255
We don't know how to put on airs.

293
00:15:13,692 --> 00:15:17,900
You know, dear, his late father sold boiled sheep's heads.

294
00:15:18,892 --> 00:15:21,360
It's not a bad job. He was a tradesman.

295
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:24,120
Sir, I think I've seen you somewhere.

296
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:26,152
Me? Yes.

297
00:15:26,292 --> 00:15:27,300
I don't think so.

298
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:28,140
Strange.

299
00:15:28,180 --> 00:15:30,480
I just can't remember where.

300
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:32,180
I've seen you somewhere.

301
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:33,700
Aren't you mistaken, madam?

302
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:35,920
No, I'm not mistaken.

303
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:36,820
Let me see.

304
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:38,215
Mouse! Mouse!

305
00:15:56,612 --> 00:15:57,782
God strike you dead!

306
00:15:57,832 --> 00:15:58,582
What do we do?

307
00:15:58,632 --> 00:16:01,582
Wait, wait, wait, will you!

308
00:16:01,632 --> 00:16:03,082
It'll go in there.

309
00:16:03,132 --> 00:16:06,307
It's going into a hole. It went into a hole.

310
00:16:15,990 --> 00:16:16,722
What could I do?

311
00:16:16,772 --> 00:16:17,982
I had to get rid of her.

312
00:16:18,032 --> 00:16:20,302
Well, what if she'd said yes?

313
00:16:20,352 --> 00:16:23,322
Nothing. I'd have taken her to San Francisco.

314
00:16:23,370 --> 00:16:24,940
That old woman?

315
00:16:24,990 --> 00:16:26,430
Not bad at all, actually.

316
00:16:26,470 --> 00:16:28,900
She had a nice, firm, plump body.

317
00:16:38,032 --> 00:16:39,777
God strike you dead!

318
00:16:43,872 --> 00:16:46,202
Don't forget San Francisco.

319
00:16:49,072 --> 00:16:52,902
Moment, moment, moment, moment... with your permission, I'll take my leave.

320
00:16:52,952 --> 00:16:54,762
Wait a few minutes.

321
00:16:54,812 --> 00:16:56,622
Got it! I've got it!

322
00:17:47,210 --> 00:17:48,010
Of what?

323
00:17:48,050 --> 00:17:48,260
No.

324
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:49,790
I'm scared of mice!

325
00:17:49,830 --> 00:17:53,830
Don't be. Uncle Asdollah pulled a trick to get rid of Farrokh Lagha.

326
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:57,450
Boy! Don't forget San Francisco.

327
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:00,132
Hurry, take her on that trip while everyone's distracted.

328
00:18:00,172 --> 00:18:00,800
Let it go.

329
00:18:00,850 --> 00:18:01,910
She's a foul-mouthed one.

330
00:18:01,950 --> 00:18:05,060
Nobody invited her, she just showed up.

331
00:18:05,110 --> 00:18:06,842
You must forgive us, madam.

332
00:18:06,892 --> 00:18:08,670
She's a foul-mouthed woman.

333
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,500
She's an old maid.

334
00:18:10,540 --> 00:18:12,680
All that frustration's gone to her head

335
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,410
and addled her brain.

336
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:16,460
It doesn't matter.

337
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:17,900
Every family has one

338
00:18:17,940 --> 00:18:20,320
of these nutcases.

339
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:22,140
Among a hundred roses,

340
00:18:22,180 --> 00:18:24,700
one thorn does no harm.

341
00:18:26,092 --> 00:18:27,212
Let's go, Mom.

342
00:18:27,252 --> 00:18:28,702
Why the rush now?

343
00:18:28,752 --> 00:18:29,520
Leaving so soon?

344
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:30,610
You're leaving too, ma'am?

345
00:18:30,660 --> 00:18:32,602
Yes, we'll take our leave, it's late.

346
00:18:32,652 --> 00:18:34,267
What a pity, honestly.

347
00:18:34,352 --> 00:18:35,642
So, what's decided?

348
00:18:36,432 --> 00:18:37,400
Aziz Khanom,

349
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:39,400
the lady's coming to our house tomorrow

350
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:42,762
to help move the furniture and clear the rooms.

351
00:18:42,812 --> 00:18:44,962
And Thursday night's best for the wedding, isn't it?

352
00:18:45,012 --> 00:18:46,462
Yes, much better.

353
00:18:46,512 --> 00:18:47,400
Congratulations.

354
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:53,400
God willing, after this wedding, we'll celebrate dear Miss Akhtar's.

355
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,400
Oh, you're too kind.

356
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:57,400
Akhtar is your humble servant, sir.

357
00:18:57,440 --> 00:19:01,240
God willing, dear, with the help of Mr. Ashdollah Mirza,

358
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:03,400
we'll marry off dear Akhtar too.

359
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:06,160
Yes, our family has plenty of young men.

360
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:09,160
God willing, one of them will ask for Miss Akhtar's hand.

361
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:10,160
Yes, yes.

362
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:14,160
Well, yes, as long as we're around, we won't leave Miss Akhtar alone.

363
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:16,160
Don't pay much mind to these old fogies.

364
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:17,640
What a darling, this Shazdeh!

365
00:19:17,680 --> 00:19:18,400
At your service.

366
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:19,400
What a son-in-law!

367
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:21,150
We've struck lucky, honestly.

368
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:23,160
Much obliged, Shazdeh, you're too kind.

369
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:26,160
Oh my, where's my bride?

370
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:28,160
Qamar dear!

371
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:29,160
Come here, darling.

372
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:31,160
They took her out.

373
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:33,160
They took her out.

374
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:36,200
Bless my pretty bride!

375
00:19:37,632 --> 00:19:40,352
Goodbye, Aziz Khanom.

376
00:19:40,852 --> 00:19:42,467
See you.

377
00:19:49,492 --> 00:19:52,522
Well, thank God, things seem to be falling into place.

378
00:19:52,572 --> 00:19:53,362
After you.

379
00:19:53,412 --> 00:19:54,062
Bless you.

380
00:19:54,112 --> 00:19:55,262
A pleasure, sir.

381
00:19:55,312 --> 00:19:56,872
Goodbye.

382
00:19:56,912 --> 00:19:57,712
Welcome.

383
00:19:57,752 --> 00:19:59,612
Well done, you.

384
00:19:59,992 --> 00:20:01,082
Bye.

385
00:20:01,132 --> 00:20:02,422
You've got a lovely face.

386
00:20:02,472 --> 00:20:03,702
Goodbye.

387
00:20:03,752 --> 00:20:04,562
So pretty.

388
00:20:04,602 --> 00:20:05,402
Goodbye.

389
00:20:05,442 --> 00:20:07,042
Come on, Akhtar. Come.

390
00:20:07,092 --> 00:20:08,022
Go safely.

391
00:20:08,072 --> 00:20:09,182
Thanks for coming.

392
00:20:09,232 --> 00:20:11,282
Mama, that old lady had a beard.

393
00:20:11,332 --> 00:20:13,012
Yes, I know.

394
00:20:15,332 --> 00:20:17,272
They weren't bad people.

395
00:20:17,672 --> 00:20:19,180
Funny townsman you've got.

396
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,220
Mash Ghasem!

397
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:21,700
Honestly, Sir, why lie?

398
00:20:21,740 --> 00:20:24,000
The grave is this close!

399
00:20:24,072 --> 00:20:25,940
Our townsman's a very good man,

400
00:20:25,980 --> 00:20:27,980
but we're terribly scared of his mother.

401
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:29,635
You'll get used to her.

402
00:20:37,152 --> 00:20:38,507
Qamar dear,

403
00:20:38,572 --> 00:20:39,860
did you like your husband?

404
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:41,720
Yes, Uncle Asdollah.

405
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:43,240
Do you love him?

406
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:46,380
Yes! So can I talk about my baby now?

407
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:48,165
Yes, darling, go ahead.

408
00:20:48,592 --> 00:20:50,960
I love my baby more than my husband.

409
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:54,080
I want to finish its red sweater tomorrow.

410
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:56,580
Did you like his sister and mother?

411
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:58,400
I liked his sister.

412
00:20:58,440 --> 00:20:59,380
I liked her too.

413
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:00,120
Me too.

414
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,660
But his mom had a beard.

415
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:03,980
Uncle Asdollah, when she kissed my face,

416
00:21:04,020 --> 00:21:04,960
it hurt.

417
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,120
Never mind, sweetie.

418
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:09,560
Daddy Dustali's going to buy her a shaving kit.

419
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:11,342
Shut up, Asdollah!

420
00:21:11,392 --> 00:21:12,600
Drop it, Dustali. Come on, Qamar.

421
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:14,680
Damn you, girl!

422
00:21:15,632 --> 00:21:17,442
I mean, God bless you!

423
00:21:21,772 --> 00:21:24,420
So, are you inviting anyone for Thursday night?

424
00:21:24,460 --> 00:21:26,440
Close family has to be there, at least.

425
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:28,700
This wedding must be held quietly.

426
00:21:28,740 --> 00:21:32,320
We could say we're in mourning and keep it quiet.

427
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:35,580
Thank God, nobody in our family has died lately.

428
00:21:35,620 --> 00:21:40,180
That Mobin-Hozour Farrokh Lagha said died, isn't he related to us?

429
00:21:40,220 --> 00:21:46,840
Mobin-Hozour was very distantly related to Farrokh Lagha's stepfather.

430
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:50,840
Forget him, given his record with the English.

431
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:53,040
Well, we have to find somebody.

432
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:57,680
Rest assured, if anyone had died, Farrokh Lagha would have told us.

433
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:59,985
What people we are!

434
00:22:00,392 --> 00:22:04,362
We can tell our relatives the groom's family is in mourning.

435
00:22:04,412 --> 00:22:05,362
Bravo.

436
00:22:05,412 --> 00:22:07,212
What a good idea, really.

437
00:22:07,252 --> 00:22:11,340
It's our own fault we offended Farrokh Lagha.

438
00:22:11,380 --> 00:22:13,220
We should have kept her sweet.

439
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:18,900
If she were here, she'd dig up a corpse for us from under a rock.

440
00:22:18,940 --> 00:22:24,700
Moment... what if Aspiran's mother calls on Uncle Mansur-ol-Saltaneh at midnight?

441
00:22:24,740 --> 00:22:26,940
He might die of fright.

442
00:22:29,352 --> 00:22:33,200
Bite your tongue! What did my poor uncle ever do to you?

443
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:34,100
They've come!

444
00:22:34,140 --> 00:22:36,100
They've come!

445
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:38,100
They've come!

446
00:22:38,140 --> 00:22:40,100
They've finally come!

447
00:22:40,140 --> 00:22:41,262
What's going on?

448
00:22:41,312 --> 00:22:44,100
I went to the railway station.

449
00:22:44,140 --> 00:22:46,100
They've come!

450
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:48,100
Who came? What's happened, Shamsali?

451
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:50,100
I'll tell you now.

452
00:22:50,140 --> 00:22:52,100
Let me catch my breath.

453
00:22:52,140 --> 00:22:55,062
What's wrong? Why so upset? Huh?

454
00:22:55,112 --> 00:22:56,100
They've come!

455
00:22:56,140 --> 00:22:58,100
They've come!

456
00:22:58,140 --> 00:23:00,100
Who came, Shamsali?

457
00:23:00,140 --> 00:23:03,990
I went to the railway station.

458
00:23:04,040 --> 00:23:06,540
Yes, yes, and then? What happened?

459
00:23:06,580 --> 00:23:08,065
I went

460
00:23:09,632 --> 00:23:11,360
to meet Pouri.

461
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:14,445
Say it, Pouri arrived and he was ill, or what?

462
00:23:15,472 --> 00:23:16,720
I didn't see Pouri.

463
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:18,480
I was late.

464
00:23:18,520 --> 00:23:20,640
I saw they'd come.

465
00:23:20,812 --> 00:23:21,602
Who?

466
00:23:21,652 --> 00:23:23,007
Who with?

467
00:23:23,072 --> 00:23:26,020
The Allies!

468
00:23:26,732 --> 00:23:28,520
The Allied army!

469
00:23:29,132 --> 00:23:30,180
They poured in!

470
00:23:30,220 --> 00:23:33,500
Allied troops poured in!

471
00:23:33,540 --> 00:23:36,580
They've occupied the railway!

472
00:23:36,620 --> 00:23:37,860
The railway?

473
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:40,920
Why the railway first of all?

474
00:23:42,092 --> 00:23:45,460
The railway installations!

475
00:23:45,500 --> 00:23:48,740
Well, they had to start somewhere.

476
00:23:49,652 --> 00:23:51,960
My poor brother, the Colonel!

477
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,800
They may arrest him...

478
00:23:53,840 --> 00:23:57,240
Sir, don't worry about them now.

479
00:23:57,280 --> 00:24:00,480
Asdollah, you're a diplomat.

480
00:24:00,520 --> 00:24:04,000
You even work at the Foreign Ministry.

481
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:11,640
But it'll be a long time before you grasp the subtleties of English policy.

482
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:13,200
Moment, moment.

483
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:16,800
You mean because your brother went to the station tonight,

484
00:24:16,840 --> 00:24:19,000
the English occupied it first of all?

485
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:22,080
It wasn't only because of him,

486
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:26,272
but it's not unrelated either.

487
00:24:26,312 --> 00:24:27,230
I see.

488
00:24:27,280 --> 00:24:31,820
I'm upset for this innocent family.

489
00:24:33,296 --> 00:24:40,740
My poor brother the Colonel never put a foot wrong in his whole life.

490
00:24:40,780 --> 00:24:46,320
Now he has to pay for my battles, unjustly and wrongly.

491
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:49,660
Suppose they did want to punish him for you,

492
00:24:49,700 --> 00:24:53,940
how did they know the Colonel was going to the station tonight?

493
00:24:53,980 --> 00:24:58,880
This Asdollah thinks they didn't recognize Pouri.

494
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:04,240
He thinks they don't know Pouri is my nephew.

495
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:08,140
Oh! How naive!

496
00:25:08,180 --> 00:25:14,340
I promise you, right now Aspiran Ghias Abadi's file

497
00:25:14,380 --> 00:25:20,980
and Qamar's wedding are on the desk of the head of the Intelligence Service.

498
00:25:21,736 --> 00:25:26,480
Mr. Asdollah Mirza still doesn't know what rotten stock the English are, Sir.

499
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:30,980
Even we, who've given the English hell for thirty years,

500
00:25:31,020 --> 00:25:33,946
still don't know them well, let alone people like...

501
00:25:33,996 --> 00:25:39,860
If I told you what I know about the English, you'd be flabbergasted.

502
00:25:40,976 --> 00:25:46,640
When the English commander was defeated by me in the Kazerun war,

503
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:49,460
he came and threw his sword at my feet.

504
00:25:49,500 --> 00:25:51,440
It seems like yesterday.

505
00:25:52,076 --> 00:25:56,040
He said, "You, with one thousand and fourteen men,

506
00:25:56,080 --> 00:26:02,160
held out against several regiments of the English army.

507
00:26:03,136 --> 00:26:08,160
This will be written in golden letters in the history of war."

508
00:26:08,816 --> 00:26:12,780
Believe me, my jaw dropped.

509
00:26:13,796 --> 00:26:18,020
A few days before, I'd counted my men myself.

510
00:26:18,060 --> 00:26:20,720
Exactly one thousand and fourteen.

511
00:26:20,760 --> 00:26:21,560
No, Sir.

512
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:23,620
There were one thousand and fifteen.

513
00:26:23,660 --> 00:26:26,920
Nonsense, one thousand and fourteen.

514
00:26:28,116 --> 00:26:30,300
Sir, God bless you, you never let us

515
00:26:30,340 --> 00:26:32,200
get a word in, Sir.

516
00:26:32,240 --> 00:26:34,040
The one who went missing

517
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:36,060
was the late Soltan Ali Khan,

518
00:26:36,100 --> 00:26:37,800
who got shot that same day.

519
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:39,880
What nonsense you talk, Ghasem!

520
00:26:39,920 --> 00:26:41,660
What difference does it make?

521
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:43,120
One thousand and fourteen.

522
00:26:43,160 --> 00:26:45,160
What do you mean, no difference!

523
00:26:45,200 --> 00:26:48,880
By Imam Ali, may God bring them to their knees!

524
00:26:49,656 --> 00:26:53,656
If not for Sir, we'd have been dead and buried seventy times over.

525
00:26:54,856 --> 00:26:57,251
May God keep him great!

526
00:26:58,256 --> 00:27:03,380
For worthless us, he threw himself into that hail of bullets.

527
00:27:03,420 --> 00:27:07,115
He threw us over his shoulder and carried us off the field.

528
00:27:07,716 --> 00:27:11,106
The English themselves were dumbstruck.

529
00:27:11,156 --> 00:27:14,340
But we saw with our own eyes that, out of fear of Sir,

530
00:27:14,380 --> 00:27:18,340
tears welled up in the Englishmen's cross eyes.

531
00:27:18,380 --> 00:27:21,340
You see, most Englishmen are cross-eyed.

532
00:27:21,380 --> 00:27:25,380
Wherever we see an Englishman, we know him by his eyes.

533
00:27:26,380 --> 00:27:31,380
Ghasem, see what the wheel of fortune does?

534
00:27:37,380 --> 00:27:43,380
They waited till their turn came round again.

535
00:27:47,076 --> 00:27:53,580
You scoundrels, what do you want with my innocent brother?

536
00:27:53,620 --> 00:28:01,580
Vile wretches, two-faced wolves, what do you want with my brother?

537
00:28:01,620 --> 00:28:05,480
Come and take your revenge on me!

538
00:28:05,520 --> 00:28:09,300
What do you want with my innocent family?

539
00:28:09,340 --> 00:28:11,500
I'm your enemy!

540
00:28:11,540 --> 00:28:14,300
Take your revenge on me!

541
00:28:28,276 --> 00:28:30,806
Wonderful, very nice.

542
00:28:30,856 --> 00:28:32,806
Looks very good in the outfit, too.

543
00:28:32,856 --> 00:28:34,136
Yes.

544
00:28:45,535 --> 00:28:46,335
Who's there? Who's there?

545
00:28:46,375 --> 00:28:48,356
Someone's knocking at the door.

546
00:28:51,356 --> 00:28:54,916
Banging with the knocker on the door.

547
00:28:57,676 --> 00:29:00,376
My heart is fluttering more and more.

548
00:29:00,416 --> 00:29:01,256
Congratulations.

549
00:29:01,296 --> 00:29:02,026
Thank you.

550
00:29:02,076 --> 00:29:04,861
God willing, you'll be a groom too.

551
00:29:17,476 --> 00:29:20,386
Brother, you're drinking a lot tonight.

552
00:29:20,436 --> 00:29:22,366
It's all right, brother.

553
00:29:22,416 --> 00:29:24,446
It's my last night in Tehran.

554
00:29:24,496 --> 00:29:27,126
So you're definitely going to Kermanshah tomorrow?

555
00:29:27,176 --> 00:29:30,346
Yes, brother, I set off tomorrow afternoon.

556
00:29:30,396 --> 00:29:33,576
I was very lucky my posting came through.

557
00:29:36,116 --> 00:29:37,766
May you have such luck too.

558
00:29:37,816 --> 00:29:39,066
Thanks.

559
00:29:39,116 --> 00:29:40,406
Sir.

560
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:42,260
Asdollah?

561
00:29:42,300 --> 00:29:44,300
Hmm, what?

562
00:29:45,156 --> 00:29:48,260
Remember my Belgian double-barreled shotgun?

563
00:29:48,300 --> 00:29:49,260
Yes?

564
00:29:49,300 --> 00:29:51,260
Yes, I remember.

565
00:29:51,300 --> 00:29:54,260
The one you liked so much.

566
00:29:54,300 --> 00:29:55,260
Remember?

567
00:29:55,300 --> 00:29:57,370
Yes, why?

568
00:29:57,636 --> 00:29:58,726
Huh? What?

569
00:29:58,776 --> 00:30:00,906
Nothing. I want to give it to you.

570
00:30:00,956 --> 00:30:02,701
But on one condition.

571
00:30:02,936 --> 00:30:04,260
What condition?

572
00:30:04,300 --> 00:30:06,500
That you do something for me.

573
00:30:07,300 --> 00:30:09,266
What?

574
00:30:09,316 --> 00:30:11,260
Here, come inside.

575
00:30:11,300 --> 00:30:13,300
All right.

576
00:30:14,416 --> 00:30:17,366
Who's there? Who's there? Someone's knocking.

577
00:30:19,036 --> 00:30:24,286
Banging with the knocker on the door.

578
00:30:24,336 --> 00:30:28,686
My heart is fluttering more and more.

579
00:30:32,104 --> 00:30:36,124
...Aspiran brings his sister and mother to live with us.

580
00:30:36,164 --> 00:30:36,964
Cheers.

581
00:30:37,004 --> 00:30:40,179
Now be a man and do something for me.

582
00:30:40,384 --> 00:30:43,260
Rent a place for his mother.

583
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:45,435
I'll pay the rent.

584
00:30:46,144 --> 00:30:49,300
I don't want his mother living with us.

585
00:30:50,264 --> 00:30:52,260
Anyway, isn't it agreed

586
00:30:52,300 --> 00:30:55,260
that Aspiran will divorce Qamar in a while?

587
00:30:55,300 --> 00:30:56,260
Yes, yes.

588
00:30:56,300 --> 00:30:58,300
So what's the point

589
00:30:58,924 --> 00:31:02,894
of uprooting his sister and mother for two or three months,

590
00:31:02,944 --> 00:31:04,260
bringing them here for what?

591
00:31:04,300 --> 00:31:06,260
Moment.

592
00:31:06,300 --> 00:31:11,700
Oh my, your drink's all gone.

593
00:31:11,740 --> 00:31:18,720
I take it you mean

594
00:31:18,760 --> 00:31:21,935
Aspiran and his sister come and stay at your place,

595
00:31:22,444 --> 00:31:25,480
but he takes his mother off somewhere and loses her.

596
00:31:25,520 --> 00:31:27,940
And he takes his sister with him too.

597
00:31:28,664 --> 00:31:30,864
Put yourself in my shoes.

598
00:31:31,564 --> 00:31:32,659
Well, well.

599
00:31:33,004 --> 00:31:34,800
Three whole months, every morning,

600
00:31:34,840 --> 00:31:38,210
first thing, laying eyes on this bearded hag.

601
00:31:38,764 --> 00:31:39,500
No, tell me,

602
00:31:39,540 --> 00:31:41,155
wouldn't it be the death of you?

603
00:31:41,620 --> 00:31:42,975
Asdollah,

604
00:31:43,764 --> 00:31:45,640
search all of Tehran,

605
00:31:45,680 --> 00:31:48,920
and you won't find a gun that handy.

606
00:31:49,584 --> 00:31:51,960
Well, I'll do my best,

607
00:31:53,524 --> 00:31:56,049
but I doubt he'll agree.

608
00:32:07,784 --> 00:32:10,124
May you be happy, God willing.

609
00:32:10,944 --> 00:32:12,324
Congratulations.

610
00:32:23,744 --> 00:32:25,879
How pretty you look!

611
00:32:33,984 --> 00:32:38,840
Someone out there dreams of holding you in his arms.

612
00:32:40,840 --> 00:32:43,840
Asi dear, where are you going?

613
00:32:44,840 --> 00:32:46,840
Come, open your mouth.

614
00:32:47,924 --> 00:32:51,840
You've done Dustali in, go see to him.

615
00:32:58,840 --> 00:32:59,800
God forgive me!

616
00:32:59,840 --> 00:33:01,800
Come, have a sweet.

617
00:33:01,840 --> 00:33:03,800
I won't, madam, I won't.

618
00:33:03,840 --> 00:33:06,235
Oh, don't be coy, eat it!

619
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:09,840
I don't like sweets with my drink.

620
00:33:15,840 --> 00:33:17,840
Fine, don't, darling.

621
00:33:18,840 --> 00:33:20,800
I'll eat it myself.

622
00:33:20,840 --> 00:33:22,800
Oh my, hello!

623
00:33:22,840 --> 00:33:24,800
Open your mouth.

624
00:33:24,840 --> 00:33:25,554
You too, Colonel dear.

625
00:33:25,604 --> 00:33:29,840
Lucky you, Dustali, what a fun family you've married into!

626
00:33:33,840 --> 00:33:36,760
The night Pouri dear didn't come, I worried till dawn.

627
00:33:36,800 --> 00:33:40,880
I kept thinking the English might have recognized you and Pouri dear

628
00:33:40,920 --> 00:33:42,680
and, God forbid, harmed you.

629
00:33:42,720 --> 00:33:45,800
I'm no child to put myself in danger.

630
00:33:45,840 --> 00:33:49,200
I went to the station in disguise.

631
00:33:49,240 --> 00:33:50,620
In a chador?

632
00:33:50,660 --> 00:33:53,160
No, you've had too much to drink again.

633
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:54,720
I went in plain clothes.

634
00:33:54,760 --> 00:33:57,805
One must be very careful these days.

635
00:33:59,204 --> 00:34:00,120
Congratulations.

636
00:34:00,170 --> 00:34:01,720
Same to you.

637
00:34:08,104 --> 00:34:13,540
Dear Uncle Napoleon, believing the English had a hand in Qamar's pregnancy,

638
00:34:13,580 --> 00:34:15,910
did not attend her wedding.

639
00:34:16,484 --> 00:34:22,640
His excuse was that a match with Aspiran Ghias Abadi was beneath our family.

640
00:34:23,604 --> 00:34:28,500
That night, fearing a possible plot, on Dear Uncle's orders,

641
00:34:29,144 --> 00:34:32,514
Mash Ghasem stood guard with a rifle until morning.

642
00:34:35,904 --> 00:34:39,440
I longed to marry off this son of mine before I died.

643
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:42,680
You see, the last time he married without telling me,

644
00:34:42,720 --> 00:34:44,640
may my tongue wither,

645
00:34:44,680 --> 00:34:46,360
I cursed him.

646
00:34:47,044 --> 00:34:49,699
My boy went to war and got shot.

647
00:34:49,804 --> 00:34:53,580
I very nearly lost my one and only son.

648
00:34:54,704 --> 00:34:58,340
After that I made so many vows, God only knows.

649
00:34:59,984 --> 00:35:02,834
Thank God, thank God.

650
00:35:02,884 --> 00:35:06,849
Knock on wood!

651
00:35:07,204 --> 00:35:13,974
After four whole months in hospital, God gave me back my boy.

652
00:35:14,024 --> 00:35:16,294
Thank God. Praise be.

653
00:35:16,344 --> 00:35:19,714
May God keep him safe for you.

654
00:35:19,764 --> 00:35:25,244
He's so kind-hearted, God always watches over him.

655
00:35:25,304 --> 00:35:27,574
I hope he'll settle down.

656
00:35:27,624 --> 00:35:31,054
You know, now that he's married Miss Qamar,

657
00:35:31,104 --> 00:35:35,454
God willing, under Mr. Khan's wing, a bad habit he has

658
00:35:35,504 --> 00:35:36,300
he'll kick it.

659
00:35:36,340 --> 00:35:38,300
There you go again, Mom.

660
00:35:38,340 --> 00:35:39,300
Oh, hush!

661
00:35:39,340 --> 00:35:42,515
Let's hope it's nothing. What bad habit?

662
00:35:42,704 --> 00:35:44,300
He must play with himself too much.

663
00:35:44,340 --> 00:35:46,340
Oh, come on!

664
00:35:47,324 --> 00:35:49,004
The things you say, Asi!

665
00:35:50,844 --> 00:35:52,284
No, dear.

666
00:35:54,824 --> 00:35:55,919
Oh!

667
00:36:08,984 --> 00:36:11,084
Oh, bless you, Asi!

668
00:36:11,584 --> 00:36:14,499
No, he doesn't have that kind of bad habit.

669
00:36:17,064 --> 00:36:24,834
You know, two or three years ago his bad friends got him hooked, as a joke.

670
00:36:24,884 --> 00:36:25,979
What?

671
00:36:26,340 --> 00:36:27,300
Hooked?

672
00:36:27,340 --> 00:36:28,300
Yes.

673
00:36:28,340 --> 00:36:30,340
Hooked on what?

674
00:36:32,184 --> 00:36:33,290
Just a pinch a day,

675
00:36:33,340 --> 00:36:35,300
two pinches at the very most.

676
00:36:35,340 --> 00:36:37,300
Once they took him to get clean,

677
00:36:37,340 --> 00:36:39,300
but he went back to it.

678
00:36:39,340 --> 00:36:42,300
Akhtar, there you go again!

679
00:36:42,340 --> 00:36:44,340
Never mind.

680
00:36:45,044 --> 00:36:46,300
Never mind, Aspiran.

681
00:36:46,340 --> 00:36:48,300
Our own donkey, Mr. Dustali Khan,

682
00:36:48,340 --> 00:36:50,300
has a puff now and then too.

683
00:36:50,340 --> 00:36:53,300
You've found yourself a nice pipe buddy, then!

684
00:36:53,340 --> 00:36:57,340
Asdollah, why talk rubbish? When did I ever smoke opium?

685
00:37:01,043 --> 00:37:03,048
Come, come this way.

686
00:37:13,944 --> 00:37:18,904
It's for your sake, or I wouldn't stay here a minute.

687
00:37:18,944 --> 00:37:20,624
You see-

688
00:37:20,684 --> 00:37:24,084
Sorry, my nerves are shot.

689
00:37:25,640 --> 00:37:27,474
I just apologize.

690
00:37:27,524 --> 00:37:28,314
Bless you.

691
00:37:28,364 --> 00:37:31,300
Brother, leave him with me tonight.

692
00:37:31,340 --> 00:37:32,434
We're going out.

693
00:37:32,484 --> 00:37:33,594
To San Francisco?

694
00:37:33,644 --> 00:37:37,300
No, we're going drinking together.

695
00:37:37,340 --> 00:37:39,300
Have fun.

696
00:37:39,340 --> 00:37:41,300
Dustali?

697
00:37:41,340 --> 00:37:43,300
I'm very sorry.

698
00:37:43,340 --> 00:37:45,300
It didn't work.

699
00:37:45,340 --> 00:37:48,244
He says he'll never leave his mother.

700
00:37:48,524 --> 00:37:49,290
Nothing sank in.

701
00:37:49,340 --> 00:37:55,694
He says they were planning to move anyway, they were house-hunting.

702
00:37:55,744 --> 00:37:58,394
You didn't talk to them the way you should have.

703
00:37:58,444 --> 00:38:01,554
I know what a rotten piece of work you are, Asdollah.

704
00:38:03,244 --> 00:38:07,754
Moment... rotten or not, I wouldn't say no to your Belgian gun.

705
00:38:07,804 --> 00:38:10,694
What can I do if he won't budge?

706
00:38:10,744 --> 00:38:12,594
Now, don't take it so hard.

707
00:38:12,644 --> 00:38:15,624
She has a beard, but it's a soft one.

708
00:38:16,224 --> 00:38:17,584
Silky.

709
00:38:18,004 --> 00:38:23,924
If you're too stingy to pay, I'll buy her a razor and brush for New Year myself.

710
00:38:23,964 --> 00:38:27,204
Damn your ugly mug, you broken-down prince!

711
00:38:28,124 --> 00:38:30,374
Moment... Dustali, don't make trouble.

712
00:38:30,424 --> 00:38:32,300
Talk rubbish and I'll tell Aspiran

713
00:38:32,340 --> 00:38:36,230
to bring his kid from his first wife here too.

714
00:38:40,904 --> 00:38:43,174
It's a long way, sir.

715
00:38:43,224 --> 00:38:46,300
Here, and all the way to Kermanshah!

716
00:38:46,340 --> 00:38:49,260
It's the department, what can you do?

717
00:38:49,300 --> 00:38:52,220
A government servant isn't his own master.

718
00:38:52,260 --> 00:38:53,900
Have fun for us, too.

719
00:38:53,940 --> 00:38:54,740
Thank you.

720
00:38:54,780 --> 00:38:57,100
Grow old together.

721
00:38:57,140 --> 00:39:00,380
Now we must go and see the place

722
00:39:01,184 --> 00:39:02,060
of our posting.

723
00:39:02,100 --> 00:39:04,690
See if we can make a life there.

724
00:39:05,024 --> 00:39:06,340
Or if we can't.

725
00:39:06,380 --> 00:39:08,680
I need a word with you.

726
00:39:08,720 --> 00:39:10,595
What do you want?

727
00:39:12,744 --> 00:39:14,294
Follow me.

728
00:39:14,864 --> 00:39:15,740
Safe travels.

729
00:39:15,780 --> 00:39:17,980
Thanks very much. No, no more for me.

730
00:39:18,020 --> 00:39:21,740
Why? Have some, for my sake. For Qamar's sake, drink!

731
00:39:21,780 --> 00:39:24,740
I never have more than one or two glashes.

732
00:39:24,780 --> 00:39:27,435
Since when are you in love, sir?

733
00:39:28,424 --> 00:39:30,039
Me? - Yes, you.

734
00:39:31,884 --> 00:39:34,740
I didn't write it. I've never written Leili a letter.

735
00:39:34,780 --> 00:39:38,280
So your daddy wrote her this letter? Huh?

736
00:39:40,780 --> 00:39:42,740
"My dear Leili.

737
00:39:42,780 --> 00:39:45,280
Do you know how much I love you?

738
00:39:45,780 --> 00:39:49,580
Do you know life without you means nothing to me?"

739
00:39:49,620 --> 00:39:50,670
Pouri, I swear...

740
00:39:50,710 --> 00:39:51,459
Listen to this.

741
00:39:51,499 --> 00:39:52,299
Shut up.

742
00:39:52,460 --> 00:39:55,980
"Ever since I heard this spluttering Arab horse

743
00:39:56,020 --> 00:39:58,600
is coming back from Ahvaz..."

744
00:39:58,640 --> 00:40:00,800
If this weren't a wedding,

745
00:40:00,840 --> 00:40:04,120
this spluttering Arab horse would smash you in the mouth

746
00:40:04,160 --> 00:40:06,100
your teeth would go down your throat.

747
00:40:06,140 --> 00:40:06,940
Pouri, I...

748
00:40:06,980 --> 00:40:10,440
I'll show you a spluttering Arab horse you'll never forget!

749
00:40:10,480 --> 00:40:11,440
Pouri, I swear by Agha Jan...

750
00:40:11,490 --> 00:40:12,494
Shut up!

751
00:40:12,544 --> 00:40:15,634
Your daddy's a beggar's spawn, just like your lowlife self.

752
00:40:15,684 --> 00:40:16,844
Yes.

753
00:40:38,460 --> 00:40:41,310
What is it? What happened? Pouri, what's wrong?

754
00:40:43,924 --> 00:40:45,334
What happened? Who was it?

755
00:40:45,384 --> 00:40:46,934
Hurry!

756
00:41:11,244 --> 00:41:12,859
Halt! Halt!

757
00:41:13,424 --> 00:41:15,114
Don't you move!

758
00:41:15,164 --> 00:41:16,434
What's up, Mash Ghasem?

759
00:41:16,484 --> 00:41:18,374
Don't you move!

760
00:41:18,424 --> 00:41:19,740
You scared me!

761
00:41:19,780 --> 00:41:21,740
Seems it's you,

762
00:41:21,780 --> 00:41:23,780
it's you, my boy.

763
00:41:25,780 --> 00:41:27,980
You scared us too.

764
00:41:39,780 --> 00:41:41,740
Asdollah, let's go.

765
00:41:41,780 --> 00:41:44,824
Couldn't you have shouted a bit more quietly?

766
00:41:44,864 --> 00:41:46,554
You think we're here on our own account?

767
00:41:46,604 --> 00:41:50,984
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie? The grave is this close!

768
00:41:52,264 --> 00:41:53,944
We're on guard duty tonight.

769
00:41:53,984 --> 00:41:55,274
Guard duty?

770
00:41:55,324 --> 00:41:59,440
Sir ordered that if any spies or whatnot show up around the garden,

771
00:41:59,480 --> 00:42:03,214
we holler so loud the whole neighborhood wakes up.

772
00:42:03,264 --> 00:42:06,354
Get away, you nearly scared me to death.

773
00:42:06,404 --> 00:42:07,730
My boy,

774
00:42:07,780 --> 00:42:11,780
say, didn't you go to Miss Qamar's wedding tonight?

775
00:42:12,604 --> 00:42:15,180
I did! I couldn't stand that spluttering Pouri.

776
00:42:15,220 --> 00:42:16,460
I came home to study.

777
00:42:16,500 --> 00:42:17,780
I see.

778
00:42:19,264 --> 00:42:20,840
Mash Ghasem, do you hear that?

779
00:42:20,880 --> 00:42:23,780
What's that noise at this hour of night?

780
00:42:24,740 --> 00:42:26,615
Muslim ibn Aqil, help us!

781
00:42:27,704 --> 00:42:30,000
Someone's trying to break the door down!

782
00:42:30,040 --> 00:42:31,915
Muslim ibn Aqil, help us!

783
00:42:35,944 --> 00:42:37,634
When I came, the door was open.

784
00:42:37,684 --> 00:42:39,169
I shut it.

785
00:42:39,524 --> 00:42:42,334
You watch our back, my boy.

786
00:42:42,384 --> 00:42:44,634
We'll go up and see what it is.

787
00:42:44,684 --> 00:42:46,169
OK, go.

788
00:42:47,544 --> 00:42:50,084
Muslim ibn Aqil, save us!

789
00:43:00,494 --> 00:43:01,740
Watch our back.

790
00:43:01,780 --> 00:43:04,045
OK, Mash Ghasem, go, don't be afraid.

791
00:43:11,554 --> 00:43:13,054
Halt!

792
00:43:20,034 --> 00:43:22,234
Saeid! Saeid!

793
00:43:22,774 --> 00:43:23,999
Saeid!

794
00:43:24,914 --> 00:43:28,974
Saeid! Saeid!

795
00:43:31,394 --> 00:43:33,714
Saeid! Saeid!

796
00:43:35,634 --> 00:43:36,859
Saeid!

797
00:43:37,780 --> 00:43:39,740
Where is he? Where's he vanished to?

798
00:43:39,780 --> 00:43:43,730
Search around here, I'll see if he went into the house.

799
00:43:43,780 --> 00:43:45,254
Saeid!

800
00:43:45,294 --> 00:43:46,094
Saeid!

801
00:43:46,134 --> 00:43:47,294
Saeid!

802
00:43:50,154 --> 00:43:51,314
Saeid!

803
00:43:54,914 --> 00:43:55,730
Saeid.

804
00:43:55,780 --> 00:43:57,780
Uncle Asdollah!

805
00:43:57,830 --> 00:43:58,623
Wh... where are you?

806
00:43:58,673 --> 00:43:59,740
Up here.

807
00:43:59,780 --> 00:44:00,740
Uncle Asdollah.

808
00:44:00,780 --> 00:44:02,740
What are you doing up there? Come down.

809
00:44:02,780 --> 00:44:05,740
Well done! You've given that boy a rupture, you devil!

810
00:44:05,780 --> 00:44:07,730
It was his fault. I didn't touch him.

811
00:44:07,780 --> 00:44:10,110
Not a bad idea, though.

812
00:44:10,414 --> 00:44:13,524
Since you don't dare go to San Francisco with Leili yourself,

813
00:44:13,574 --> 00:44:17,344
you've blocked poor Pouri's road to San Francisco, you rascal!

814
00:44:17,394 --> 00:44:19,740
Uncle Asdollah, please, is Pouri hurt?

815
00:44:19,780 --> 00:44:23,200
Honestly, no, he just fainted in the hallway.

816
00:44:23,470 --> 00:44:26,400
When I came, his father had gone for Dr. Naser-ol-Hokama.

817
00:44:26,450 --> 00:44:27,684
What was the fight about?

818
00:44:27,734 --> 00:44:30,864
He'd stolen the letter I wrote to Leili.

819
00:44:30,914 --> 00:44:33,374
And he swore at Agha Jan, really foully.

820
00:44:33,554 --> 00:44:36,584
Uncle Asdollah, he didn't show my letter to Uncle Colonel?

821
00:44:36,634 --> 00:44:37,584
No.

822
00:44:37,634 --> 00:44:39,364
Tell me the truth, Uncle Asdollah.

823
00:44:39,414 --> 00:44:43,084
No, he was just telling his father something, then he fainted.

824
00:44:43,134 --> 00:44:45,794
Better lie low for a while till we see what happens.

825
00:44:45,834 --> 00:44:47,304
Come on down, now.

826
00:44:47,354 --> 00:44:48,204
Is Agha Jan here?

827
00:44:48,254 --> 00:44:49,184
He won't hurt you.

828
00:44:49,234 --> 00:44:50,934
Come down.

829
00:44:53,734 --> 00:44:55,384
You've made a mess of it, you clumsy donkey!

830
00:44:55,434 --> 00:44:56,740
You've got us all in trouble.

831
00:44:56,780 --> 00:44:59,740
The Colonel's sworn to get you.

832
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:01,740
I think you're in for it.

833
00:45:01,780 --> 00:45:04,740
Now do you see the way I suggested was the best?

834
00:45:04,780 --> 00:45:05,740
What way?

835
00:45:05,780 --> 00:45:07,424
San Francisco.

836
00:45:07,474 --> 00:45:09,479
You brainless son of a dog!

837
00:45:09,534 --> 00:45:10,740
Fighting won't help.

838
00:45:10,780 --> 00:45:14,740
If someone cursed your father, you'd get angry too!

839
00:45:14,780 --> 00:45:16,780
He slapped me first.

840
00:45:16,830 --> 00:45:21,774
Son of a dog! With that kick to the boy's privates, he'll be lucky to survive.

841
00:45:22,774 --> 00:45:27,024
When I examined him while he was out, it was swollen like a pumpkin.

842
00:45:27,074 --> 00:45:28,324
What's it to me?

843
00:45:28,374 --> 00:45:29,444
Well, he hit me too.

844
00:45:29,494 --> 00:45:31,954
And now he talks back!

845
00:45:32,874 --> 00:45:34,244
Now, don't get angry.

846
00:45:34,294 --> 00:45:35,284
Was it serious?

847
00:45:35,334 --> 00:45:37,599
They need to take him to hospital.

848
00:45:39,874 --> 00:45:42,844
Agha Jan, Agha Jan, believe me, he's lying, Agha Jan!

849
00:45:42,894 --> 00:45:44,934
Oh sure, he's lying, of course.

850
00:45:44,974 --> 00:45:46,524
Don't talk rubbish.

851
00:45:46,780 --> 00:45:49,740
I saw the letter you wrote to Leili in his fist.

852
00:45:49,780 --> 00:45:52,740
You dog, if your uncle gets it, he'll wipe out our whole family!

853
00:45:52,780 --> 00:45:54,740
What's this spluttering Pouri got to do with me?

854
00:45:54,780 --> 00:45:57,740
He deserved that beating. He asked for it.

855
00:45:57,780 --> 00:46:00,740
Shut up, you shameless boy! The Colonel's hunting for you

856
00:46:00,780 --> 00:46:02,740
to put two bullets in your empty skull.

857
00:46:02,780 --> 00:46:03,864
Two bullets in me?

858
00:46:03,914 --> 00:46:05,764
No, young man, in mine, then!

859
00:46:05,814 --> 00:46:10,524
Anger won't help. Tomorrow I'll try to smooth things over with the Colonel.

860
00:46:10,574 --> 00:46:12,224
Pouri hasn't shown Saeid's letter to anyone?

861
00:46:12,274 --> 00:46:13,954
No, not yet.

862
00:46:14,014 --> 00:46:16,444
We should've pinched the letter somehow.

863
00:46:16,494 --> 00:46:18,109
Well, it didn't work out.

864
00:46:18,434 --> 00:46:20,704
Then I doubt they'll ever tell Sir.

865
00:46:20,754 --> 00:46:22,084
Don't worry, they'll try

866
00:46:22,134 --> 00:46:23,784
to hush up the letter business.

867
00:46:23,834 --> 00:46:24,740
Their reputation's at stake.

868
00:46:24,780 --> 00:46:26,740
Yes, maybe.

869
00:46:26,780 --> 00:46:28,740
But if this boy ends up crippled,

870
00:46:28,780 --> 00:46:30,740
then this donkey and I are morally responsible.

871
00:46:30,780 --> 00:46:33,580
Not just morally, legally too.

872
00:46:33,620 --> 00:46:35,980
Just be sensible until it all blows over.

873
00:46:36,020 --> 00:46:37,780
They're not the suing kind.

874
00:46:37,820 --> 00:46:40,940
Aristocrats think it beneath them to set foot in court.

875
00:46:40,980 --> 00:46:45,100
If anything happens to poor Pouri, things will get very ugly.

876
00:46:45,140 --> 00:46:49,980
Saeid, why not spend a few days in Dezashib with Rahim Khan's kids?

877
00:46:50,020 --> 00:46:51,740
No, let me stay, I must be with Leili.

878
00:46:51,780 --> 00:46:53,080
Shut it! After the disgrace you caused?

879
00:46:53,120 --> 00:46:54,040
Don't get angry.

880
00:46:54,080 --> 00:46:55,200
Listen, kid.

881
00:46:55,240 --> 00:46:58,030
We know what's best better than you.

882
00:46:58,080 --> 00:47:01,200
As it happens, I'm having lunch at Rahim Khan's tomorrow.

883
00:47:01,240 --> 00:47:03,200
I'll call him from here right now.

884
00:47:03,240 --> 00:47:05,200
No, they're asleep now.

885
00:47:05,240 --> 00:47:07,200
Don't wake them at this hour,

886
00:47:07,240 --> 00:47:08,200
they'll worry.

887
00:47:08,240 --> 00:47:10,200
It's nothing serious, it's fine.

888
00:47:10,240 --> 00:47:11,200
Rahim Khan will love it.

889
00:47:11,240 --> 00:47:12,855
Uncle Asdollah.

890
00:47:13,240 --> 00:47:15,765
Don't be scared, your dad won't hurt you.

891
00:47:21,780 --> 00:47:23,780
Saeid.

892
00:47:47,454 --> 00:47:48,679
Saeid.

893
00:47:56,374 --> 00:47:59,614
Since when have you had a thing with Leili?

894
00:48:00,354 --> 00:48:02,489
Since the thirteenth of Mordad.

895
00:48:02,994 --> 00:48:07,744
Bravo. How precise. Well done.

896
00:48:08,634 --> 00:48:10,684
I suppose you know the hour too?

897
00:48:10,734 --> 00:48:13,574
Three o'clock. Quarter to three.

898
00:48:21,454 --> 00:48:24,369
You haven't gone all the way with her, have you?

899
00:48:24,954 --> 00:48:27,540
No, I just wrote her a few letters.

900
00:48:27,580 --> 00:48:29,340
Does she love you too?

901
00:48:29,380 --> 00:48:30,540
Very much.

902
00:48:30,734 --> 00:48:33,040
Well, tell me, what have you done?

903
00:48:33,080 --> 00:48:34,480
We haven't promised anything yet.

904
00:48:34,520 --> 00:48:35,800
No, you dumb calf!

905
00:48:35,840 --> 00:48:40,780
As Asdollah Mirza says, have you been to San Francisco together or not?

906
00:48:42,014 --> 00:48:43,304
Have you?

907
00:48:43,514 --> 00:48:44,520
Have you or not?

908
00:48:44,560 --> 00:48:46,380
What kind of talk is that! Me...

909
00:48:46,420 --> 00:48:47,440
Leili and me...

910
00:48:47,480 --> 00:48:49,540
Don't play coy. Yes or no?

911
00:48:49,580 --> 00:48:50,380
Go on, say it.

912
00:48:50,420 --> 00:48:52,640
Agha Jan, I love Leili very much.

913
00:48:52,680 --> 00:48:53,600
Spineless!

914
00:48:53,640 --> 00:48:55,500
No, I'm only joking, son.

915
00:48:55,540 --> 00:48:58,320
Leili's engaged to her cousin. You won't get her.

916
00:48:58,360 --> 00:49:00,625
Leili can't stand Pouri.

917
00:49:01,690 --> 00:49:03,440
Didn't I say Rahim Khan would be delighted?

918
00:49:03,480 --> 00:49:04,260
Where's Saeid?

919
00:49:04,300 --> 00:49:07,865
The poor kid is really down. Go cheer him up somehow.

920
00:50:08,710 --> 00:50:09,870
What's wrong?

921
00:50:10,750 --> 00:50:12,400
Nothing. Agha Jan calls me spineless.

922
00:50:12,450 --> 00:50:13,610
Why?

923
00:50:14,350 --> 00:50:18,190
He says I'm spineless because I haven't... done the thing with Leili.

924
00:50:18,230 --> 00:50:19,030
I mean, gone.

925
00:50:19,070 --> 00:50:20,620
Gone where?

926
00:50:21,410 --> 00:50:22,800
You know, the thing.

927
00:50:22,850 --> 00:50:26,540
The one you keep talking about.

928
00:50:26,590 --> 00:50:27,815
Bravo!

929
00:50:30,150 --> 00:50:32,230
Hats off to your Agha Jan!

930
00:50:33,010 --> 00:50:34,885
He's got a good plan.

931
00:50:38,150 --> 00:50:39,900
But it's a pity you're

932
00:50:40,150 --> 00:50:42,025
so spineless.

933
00:50:42,310 --> 00:50:43,460
Uncle Asdollah, if I...

934
00:50:43,510 --> 00:50:44,800
If...

935
00:50:45,970 --> 00:50:46,950
If what?

936
00:50:46,990 --> 00:50:48,280
If...

937
00:50:48,730 --> 00:50:49,940
If what?

938
00:50:49,980 --> 00:50:50,780
If...

939
00:50:50,820 --> 00:50:51,780
Get married?

940
00:50:51,820 --> 00:50:53,280
No, Uncle Asdollah.

941
00:50:53,320 --> 00:50:53,980
Hm?

942
00:50:54,020 --> 00:50:55,320
Then what?

943
00:50:56,820 --> 00:50:57,980
Go on, say it.

944
00:50:58,020 --> 00:50:59,520
I...

945
00:51:00,520 --> 00:51:04,150
What must I do so they don't give Leili to Pouri?

946
00:51:10,940 --> 00:51:14,440
Bravo! Now you're finally talking like a grown man.

947
00:51:14,480 --> 00:51:17,440
I've told you a hundred times, take her to San Francisco.

948
00:51:17,480 --> 00:51:20,440
No, Uncle Asdollah, I mean...

949
00:51:20,480 --> 00:51:23,480
Moment, cold feet again, you wimp?

950
00:51:24,330 --> 00:51:27,480
No, but how?

951
00:51:32,480 --> 00:51:35,440
Got any colored pencils? - Yes.

952
00:51:35,480 --> 00:51:39,440
Go get them. Bring a purple one and a nice pink one,

953
00:51:39,480 --> 00:51:42,525
so I can draw you a picture. - Uncle Asdollah!

954
00:51:44,480 --> 00:51:48,480
All right, I'll do one myself in crayon and send it to you.

955
00:51:51,480 --> 00:51:54,265
Why are your legs wet, sir?

956
00:51:54,480 --> 00:51:55,575
It's water.

